    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n10544" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">consōlābĭlis</span></b> ,
			e, adj.
		consolor, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>pertaining to consolation</i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>Pass., that may be consoled, consolable</i> (very
			rare): dolor, vix, * <i><span class="en">Cic. Fam. 4,
				3, 2</span></i>.—<i>Comp.</i>,
					<i><span class="en">Ambros. Ep.
			8</span></i>.—* </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>Act., that brings consolation, consolatory</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">carmen,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Gell. 16, 19, 12</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
